---
/**
 * Capture Chromium's one-shot install prompt before the island hydrates.
 *
 * `beforeinstallprompt` fires once, after the page has loaded, and the game's
 * Options screen can be several hundred kilobytes of JavaScript away. This inline
 * listener is in the head on every page, so the event is kept even when React has
 * not mounted yet; `src/components/game/pwa/install.ts` adopts the stash when it
 * starts watching. `preventDefault` is what suppresses Chromium's own mini-infobar,
 * which is the only way to show the prompt from the game's own Install button.
 *
 * Inline on purpose: a bundled module is deferred, which is the race this exists to
 * remove. The CSP already allows inline scripts (`script-src 'unsafe-inline'`).
 */
---

<script is:inline>
  window.addEventListener("beforeinstallprompt", (event) => {
    event.preventDefault();
    window.__everythingstarInstallPrompt = event;
  });
</script>
